<http://data.silknow.org/object/0a1d27fd-7d9b-3264-905d-b0e1da98a54a>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Plain weave cotton embroidered with silk in surface darning on the diagonal and running stitch with a facing of woven silk and a backing of silk satin.\nThe central field has a yellow ground and is decorated with 5 complete rows of geometric motifs.  Row [1] has an 8-pointed star in either dark blue with a red diamond in the centre or a red star with a green diamond.  Brackets at the corners form an interrupted square around the star. This motif alternates with a white horizontal cartouche with a small vertical green cartouche, blue diamond and horizontal arch-shaped segments.\nRow [2] has a light blue vertical cartouche like the cartouche in row [1] but in different colours alternating with a blue pointed square containing a light yellow star.  Black lines from the corner of this pointed square join the corners of the dark blue or red stars.  The border has a very pale grey ground with a lobed diamond in yellow alternating with a lobed cartouche in pink.\nFacing: bias-cut dark blue silk with a fine light blue irregular check.\nBacking: pieced; green satin.\nEmbroidery Thread: 2S silk; black [outlines], shades of red sometimes faded to pink, yellow, light blue, blue, dark blue, green, white, pale grey, greenish-beige, light brown."@en , "Middle East, Textile; Panel, silk-embroidered cotton, grid design of star-medallions and cartouches on yellow ground, Azerbaijan or NW Iran, 1750-1800"@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/30b00c32-9bd2-3c64-b1dd-677d264d23a6> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/7c11706b-5819-35bc-a9e8-300b4204e8f9> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/01a1ebc2-7d07-3b2e-a15a-aa6618ae7f4b> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Plain weave cotton embroidered with silk in surface darning on the diagonal and running stitch with a facing of woven silk and a backing of silk satin.\nThe central field has a yellow ground and is decorated with 5 complete rows of geometric motifs.  Row [1] has an 8-pointed star in either dark blue with a red diamond in the centre or a red star with a green diamond.  Brackets at the corners form an interrupted square around the star. This motif alternates with a white horizontal cartouche with a small vertical green cartouche, blue diamond and horizontal arch-shaped segments.\nRow [2] has a light blue vertical cartouche like the cartouche in row [1] but in different colours alternating with a blue pointed square containing a light yellow star.  Black lines from the corner of this pointed square join the corners of the dark blue or red stars.  The border has a very pale grey ground with a lobed diamond in yellow alternating with a lobed cartouche in pink.\nFacing: bias-cut dark blue silk with a fine light blue irregular check.\nBacking: pieced; green satin.\nEmbroidery Thread: 2S silk; black [outlines], shades of red sometimes faded to pink, yellow, light blue, blue, dark blue, green, white, pale grey, greenish-beige, light brown."@en , "Middle East, Textile; Panel, silk-embroidered cotton, grid design of star-medallions and cartouches on yellow ground, Azerbaijan or NW Iran, 1750-1800"@en ;
        ecrm:P43_has_dimension         <http://data.silknow.org/object/0a1d27fd-7d9b-3264-905d-b0e1da98a54a/dimension/2> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/0a1d27fd-7d9b-3264-905d-b0e1da98a54a/dimension/1> ;
        dc:identifier                  "T.39-1940" ;
        <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs>
                <https://collections.vam.ac.uk/item/O153840> .

