        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Plain weave cotton embroidered with silk in surface darning on the diagonal and running stitch with a facing of woven silk and a backing of silk satin.\nThe central field has a yellow ground and is decorated with 5 complete rows of geometric motifs.  Row [1] has an 8-pointed star in either dark blue with a red diamond in the centre or a red star with a green diamond.  Brackets at the corners form an interrupted square around the star. This motif alternates with a white horizontal cartouche with a small vertical green cartouche, blue diamond and horizontal arch-shaped segments.\nRow [2] has a light blue vertical cartouche like the cartouche in row [1] but in different colours alternating with a blue pointed square containing a light yellow star.  Black lines from the corner of this pointed square join the corners of the dark blue or red stars.  The border has a very pale grey ground with a lobed diamond in yellow alternating with a lobed cartouche in pink.\nFacing: bias-cut dark blue silk with a fine light blue irregular check.\nBacking: pieced; green satin.\nEmbroidery Thread: 2S silk; black [outlines], shades of red sometimes faded to pink, yellow, light blue, blue, dark blue, green, white, pale grey, greenish-beige, light brown."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/0a1d27fd-7d9b-3264-905d-b0e1da98a54a> .

